Snapshot 2026-09-25 (i265): sse / variance_diff row overhead (v3 tier).

Same cell and finding shape as perf_residual_pd0scratch_2026-09-25.meta: at
1024x1024 gradient qp40 p10 (still) the port's `variance::sse` ran 13,584
calls at 796 Ir/call against C's `svt_spatial_full_distortion_kernel_avx2` at
13,584 calls and 194 Ir/call. Per-row slicing, a zero-length scalar tail loop
and a drain counter cost more than the arithmetic.

- sse (v3): blocks of at most 128x128 (per-lane i32 sums cannot overflow:
  width*height/8 squares of at most 255^2 = 1.07e9) skip the drain; 16-wide
  and multiple-of-32 widths walk rows with no per-row range arithmetic.
  A max-difference test at the ceiling (16x1024, 32x512, 64x256, 128x128) was
  added next to the existing drain cases.
- variance_diff (v3): widths that are multiples of 16 walk whole rows the same
  way, with no scalar tail.

output: byte-identical (.obu cmp at the profiled cell)

callgrind Ir, 1024 p10:
  sse            10,812,112 -> 6,571,776
  variance_diff   6,988,512 -> 4,665,024
  total         336,290,577 -> 329,726,815   (-1.95%)
